<urn:atm:triage:finding/BB3-005>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "BB3-005" ;
  triage:title "D6 revision-distinctness test gives false assurance; doc-named tests broadly don't assert their doc line" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr QA1-B4 + fenix critical review I1, reviewed at 27e21224c. scripts/tests/test_render_procedure_pages.py::test_two_revisions_render_distinct_step_tables (L25-29) asserts only that whole-page text differs, true trivially via title/date scalars, and never isolates the Steps-table markup itself -- so it passes despite the byte-identical tables in BB3-001. The same doc-named-presence-not-coverage pattern recurs broadly: .just/tests/test_generate_report_index.py:62-70,65-66 (asserts field membership, not real index content); scripts/tests/test_render_procedure_pages.py:31-33 (hits the wrong missing-mermaid-flow path, not the entry-without-section path at render_procedure_pages.py:168-169), :39-47,55-56 (check=True on a clean tree detects nothing stale); source-text greps in scripts/smoke/test_run_feature_smoke.py:30-31, scripts/phase-ai/test_run_hermes_graft_live.py:26-29, scripts/smoke/test_colima_skill_report.py:69-71. Each test name promises verification the implementation does not provide." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "test-coverage" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "qa" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "scripts/tests/test_render_procedure_pages.py" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-12T19:19:46Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Routed to cipher's BB3-FIX-R1. Fix needs a D6 test that actually isolates and diffs the Steps-table fragment, plus fixture-based rewrites of the other doc-named tests listed. REOPENED as Blocking (BB3-QA2 B1, 2026-09-12T20:20:11Z): cipher's BB3-FIX-R1 replaced the assertion but test_two_revisions_render_distinct_step_tables (scripts/tests/test_render_procedure_pages.py:41-45) now compares a non-discriminating revision pair (7475fed9 / 93458691, byte-identical apart from the revision hash itself) -- the test is still hollow, just differently. Fix must use a genuinely step-differing pair (e.g. 513b3374 vs 93458691) or assert directly on row-count/case-name-set. Routed to cipher's BB3-FIX-R2 (fix/bb3-qa2-r2, per fenix's fix-round-worktree ruling 2026-09-12T20:24:40Z). BB3-QA3 (2026-09-12T21:08:20Z): confirmed genuinely fixed via real HTMLParser-based table-row parsing (_TableProbe), comparing 93458691 (26 rows) vs 513b3374 (27 rows) with a GRAFT-001 marker present only in the newer revision; verified against actual doc content, not just the test assertions." ;
  triage:relatedFinding "BB3-001" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-12T19:19:46Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB3-005/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/BB3-005/2> ;
  triage:hasResolution <urn:atm:triage:resolution/BB3-005/1> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-12T21:08:20Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "3" .

